
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

Focused native Home Key web checks (run from the project root):

clang++ -std=c++17 -Itest\homekey_web\stubs -Ilib\OFM-Network\src -Ilib\OFM-HomeKey\src test\homekey_web\web_request_test.cpp lib\OFM-Network\src\OpenKNX\Network\Webserver\WebRequest.cpp -o homekey-web-test.exe
.\homekey-web-test.exe

npm install --prefix test\homekey_web --ignore-scripts
npm test --prefix test\homekey_web

These check the unmodified Network request body API, exact 42/50-byte framing,
valid/invalid eight-digit setup codes, existing-code comparison, first setup,
five-attempt cooldown, reboot/wraparound policy, MAC-derived setup IDs and form
behavior. QR checks use an independent jsQR decoder to verify scannability and
the exact HomeKit payload, including leading-zero codes, IP flag and lock
category. They also verify local-only generation, gating and secret clearing.
The UI test uses a mock DOM/device. On-device NVS persistence, actual HTTP
operation and iPhone scanning/Apple pairing still require hardware validation.
